.Dd March 2, 2026
.Dt AS 1
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm as
.Nd Substrate assembler frontend
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 32 | Fl 64 | Fl -32 | Fl -64
.Op Fl c
.Op Fl g
.Op Fl I Ar dir
.Op Fl D Ar macro Ns Op = Ns Ar value
.Op Fl march Ar cpu
.Op Fl mtune Ar cpu
.Op Fl msyntax Ns = Ns Ar att|intel
.Op Fl W | Fl -warn | Fl -no-warn | Fl -fatal-warnings
.Op Fl al Ns Op = Ns Ar file
.Op Fl -defsym Ar sym=val
.Op Fl -statistics
.Op Fl -target-help
.Op Fl Wa Ar opts
.Op Fl -max-input-bytes Ar n
.Op Fl -max-line-bytes Ar n
.Op Fl -max-token-length Ar n
.Op Fl -max-macro-depth Ar n
.Op Fl -max-include-depth Ar n
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Ar input.s
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the Substrate assembler command-line frontend.
It provides GNU-compatible assembler option handling, source preflight limits,
and ELF post-validation through
.Xr libelfobj 3 .
.Pp
Current release behavior is a hybrid pipeline:
.Nm
forwards final assembly to a backend assembler toolchain
.Pq usually via Xr gcc 1
and then validates output object invariants
.Pq ET_REL, class, and machine .
In-tree native parser/encoder/relocation modules are staged and continuously
validated by the assembler test suite.
.Pp
Alias binaries
.Nm as.x86
and
.Nm as.x64
select 32-bit and 64-bit defaults respectively.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--max-token-length"
.It Fl 32 , Fl -32
Select 32-bit mode (i386 output contract).
.It Fl 64 , Fl -64
Select 64-bit mode (x86-64 output contract).
.It Fl c
Accepted for compatibility; output remains an object file.
.It Fl g
Request debug-capable assembly output from backend.
.It Fl I Ar dir
Add include search path.
.It Fl D Ar macro Ns Op = Ns Ar value
Define preprocessor symbol.
.It Fl march Ar cpu
Select target machine/ISA level string.
.It Fl mtune Ar cpu
Select tuning target string.
.It Fl msyntax Ns = Ns Ar att|intel
Select x86 syntax mode.
.It Fl W , Fl -warn
Enable warnings.
.It Fl -no-warn
Disable warnings.
.It Fl -fatal-warnings
Treat warnings as errors.
.It Fl al Ns Op = Ns Ar file
Emit listing output.
If
.Ar file
is omitted, listing path defaults to
.Ar output
with
.Pa .lst
suffix.
.It Fl -defsym Ar sym=val
Define absolute assembler symbol.
.It Fl -statistics
Print wall-clock/resource usage statistics.
.It Fl -target-help
Print target summary and exit.
.It Fl Wa Ar opts
Pass comma-separated options to backend assembler.
.It Fl -max-input-bytes Ar n
Reject source larger than
.Ar n
bytes.
.It Fl -max-line-bytes Ar n
Reject logical lines larger than
.Ar n
bytes.
.It Fl -max-token-length Ar n
Reject tokens larger than
.Ar n
bytes.
.It Fl -max-macro-depth Ar n
Reject macro nesting deeper than
.Ar n .
.It Fl -max-include-depth Ar n
Reject include nesting deeper than
.Ar n .
.El
.Sh DIRECTIVES
.Nm
tracks GNU-style directive families used by Substrate userland and toolchain flows,
including:
.Bl -tag -width ".cfi_startproc/.cfi_endproc"
.It Data
.Cm .byte , .short/.hword , .long/.int , .quad/.8byte , .float , .double ,
.Cm .ascii , .asciz/.string , .zero/.space , .fill , .skip , .org , .incbin
.It Sections and layout
.Cm .text , .data , .bss , .rodata , .section , .pushsection , .popsection ,
.Cm .previous , .subsection , .group , .align/.balign/.p2align
.It Symbols
.Cm .globl/.global , .local , .weak , .comm , .lcomm , .type , .size ,
.Cm .hidden , .protected , .internal , .symver
.It Conditionals and macros
.Cm .if/.ifdef/.ifndef/.else/.endif , .macro/.endm , .rept/.endr , .irp/.irpc
.It Debug/CFI
.Cm .file , .loc , .cfi_*
.El
.Sh ARCHITECTURE SYNTAX
.Bl -tag -width "AArch64 (ARMv8.0-v8.1)"
.It x86 / x86-64
AT&T syntax is default.
Intel syntax is available with
.Fl msyntax=intel .
ISA-level gating is controlled by
.Fl march
.Pq x86-64-v1/v2/v3/v4 .
.It ARMv7 (AArch32)
Staged support includes
.Cm .arm/.thumb/.thumb_func ,
condition codes, IT blocks, register lists,
VFP/NEON forms, and ARM relocation mappings.
.It AArch64 (ARMv8.0-v8.1)
Staged support includes A64 data-processing/branch/load-store/system,
SIMD/FP, ARMv8.1 LSE/RDMA/LOR/system-register patterns,
and AArch64 relocation mappings.
.El
.Pp
See
.Pa docs/specs/as_arch_reference.md
for the per-architecture instruction-family appendix.
.Sh NOTE.GNU.PROPERTY
For x86-64 ISA level tagging,
.Nm
uses
.Pa .note.gnu.property
with GNU property type
.Dv GNU_PROPERTY_X86_ISA_1_NEEDED
.Pq 0xc0008002 .
The ISA bitmask uses:
.Bl -tag -width GNU_PROPERTY_X86_ISA_1_BASELINE
.It Dv GNU_PROPERTY_X86_ISA_1_BASELINE
Baseline x86-64 ISA.
.It Dv GNU_PROPERTY_X86_ISA_1_V2
x86-64-v2 requirement bit.
.It Dv GNU_PROPERTY_X86_ISA_1_V3
x86-64-v3 requirement bit.
.It Dv GNU_PROPERTY_X86_ISA_1_V4
x86-64-v4 requirement bit.
.El
When the selected/used ISA level is v2+,
.Nm
marks the highest required level via cumulative needed bits.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width AS_BACKEND
.It Ev AS_BACKEND
Backend compiler/assembler driver path.
If unset,
.Nm
uses
.Ev CC
or falls back to
.Dq gcc .
.It Ev AS_ERROR_CODES
If non-empty,
.Nm
prefixes driver-originated diagnostics with stable internal error IDs.
.It Ev AS_MAX_INPUT_BYTES
Default for
.Fl -max-input-bytes .
.It Ev AS_MAX_LINE_BYTES
Default for
.Fl -max-line-bytes .
.It Ev AS_MAX_TOKEN_LENGTH
Default for
.Fl -max-token-length .
.It Ev AS_MAX_MACRO_DEPTH
Default for
.Fl -max-macro-depth .
.It Ev AS_MAX_INCLUDE_DEPTH
Default for
.Fl -max-include-depth .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width "123"
.It 0
Successful assembly and validation.
.It 1
Backend execution, validation, or internal frontend failure.
.It 2
Usage/argument error.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "docs/specs/as_arch_reference.md"
.It Pa docs/specs/as_spec.md
Assembler formal specification.
.It Pa docs/specs/as_rollout.md
Rollout and release gating matrix.
.It Pa docs/specs/as_arch_reference.md
Per-architecture instruction-family appendix.
.El
